  1. Source Code.

  The "source code" for a work means the preferred form of the work for
making modifications to it.  "Object code" means any non-source form of a
work.

  A "Standard Interface" means an interface that either is an official
standard defined by a recognized standards body, or, in the case of
interfaces specified for a particular programming language, one that
is widely used among developers working in that language.

  The "System Libraries" of an executable work include anything, other
than the work as a whole, that (a) is included in a normal bundle of
components included in the work's design as a component primarily
designed for use in specifying or customizing the work's interfaces,
and (b) is not part of the work's own source code.

  "Installation Information" for an executable work means anything,
other than the work as a whole, that (a) is specifically included in
the work for the purpose of being used together with that work, and
(b) is sufficient in quantity and functionality to allow the work to
be installed and re-executed using modified source code from the
work.  "Installation Information" does not include anything that
would be required to interface with any subsequent modified version
of the work that does not require the Installation Information.

